---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

/*
 * Privacy notice. It describes only what this site actually runs: Vercel
 * hosting and Web Analytics, the theme choice in
 * localStorage, and the email / Cal.com / LinkedIn ways to get in touch. When
 * any of those change, update the
 * matching section and the date.
 */
const updated = "22 November 2026";
const email = "contact@vican.design";
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy |"
	description="What happens with your data when you visit vican.design: hosting, visitor statistics, fonts and getting in touch."
>
	<article class="w-full max-w-7xl mx-auto py-[var(--section-gap)]">
		<div class="container mx-auto px-4">
			<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[66ch]">
				<h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl text-palette-brightest-white">Privacy</h1>
				<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-secondary-foreground">Last updated {updated}</p>

				<div class="prose mt-10">
					<p>
						This website is my portfolio. It has no accounts, no forms and no ads, and it
						doesn't set any cookies. This page explains the little that does happen with
						your data when you visit.
					</p>

					<h2>Who is responsible</h2>
					<p>
						Marek Vicáň, reachable at <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>. Write to
						this address with any question about your data.
					</p>

					<h2>Hosting</h2>
					<p>
						The site runs on Vercel. Like every web server, theirs receives your IP address,
						your browser type and the time of your visit, which it needs to deliver the page
						and keep the site secure. Vercel may process this data outside the EU, under the
						safeguards the GDPR requires.
					</p>

					<h2>Visitor statistics</h2>
					<p>
						I use Vercel Web Analytics to see which pages people read. It works without
						cookies and doesn't follow you across other websites. I only see totals, such as
						page views, the site you came from, your country and the type of device. The legal
						basis is my legitimate interest in knowing which parts of the site are useful
						(Article 6(1)(f) GDPR).
					</p>

					<h2>Getting in touch</h2>
					<p>
						If you email me, I use your address and message only to reply and to keep our
						conversation. If you book a call, the booking runs through Cal.com, which shares
						your name, email and anything you write with me, under
						<a href="https://cal.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Cal.com's privacy policy</a>.
						The LinkedIn link takes you to LinkedIn, where their own rules apply.
					</p>

					<h2>Saved in your browser</h2>
					<p>
						If you switch between light and dark mode, the choice is saved in your browser's
						local storage so the site remembers it next time. It never leaves your device.
					</p>

					<h2>Your rights</h2>
					<p>
						You can ask me what data I have about you, and ask me to correct or delete it or
						to stop using it. Just email me. You can also complain to the data protection
						authority in your country.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>
